# verbatim: characters 32 (space) .. 126 (~), 16 bytes per glyph, one byte per
# scanline, MSB = leftmost pixel. 95 glyphs x 16 = 1520 bytes.
#
# Compile (kernel emit mode):
#   python src/user/grithl/compiler/gritc.py #       src/kernel/grithlk/font.ghl -o build/ghl/font.asm #       -L src/user/grithl/lib --embed --target kernel --forbid-asm
#
# NOTE: gritc `data` lands in the writable .data region (vs the asm's .rodata).
# The glyph table is never written; this is the same placement crypto.ghl's
# constant tables already use. Consumers (gui/render.asm) reference font_data as
# a forward ref in the single kernel NASM TU.
# ============================================================================

